a good makeup artist can transform even  the most  recognizable actor into a weird  wonderful  or terrifying alien and make them pretty  much  unrecognizable in the process here's  what these movie aliens look like  without their makeup  lee pace has appeared in a whole bunch  of movies and tv shows over the years  but arguably  his most high profile role is ronan the  accuser  the alien villain of the 2014 marvel  film guardians of the galaxy  in the comics ronan is part of the blue  skinned alien species known as the cree  so makeup artists elizabeth yanny jorju  and david white  had to paint pace's whole body blue and  almost entirely shroud his face in black  tar  while promoting the film pace told the  youtube channel screenslam that he  actually  loved wearing his extensive makeup  because it serves as a  mask for the character he explained i  move my face  in a different way but what's great  about that too is that it's not the way  the character looks it's the way he  wants to look he's got blue skin but on  top of that  he's painted this fearsome mask because  that's how he wants to present himself  to the world  yanni giorgio and white also designed  the look for other extraterrestrial  characters in the film  which earned them an oscar nomination  for best makeup and hair styling in  2015.  as for pace he went on to play ronin  again in 2019's captain marvel  for going the black face paint since the  movie takes place before guardians  and features a less radicalized version  of the character  french actress maiwen labesco known  anonymously as maiwen  portrayed the tall and mysterious alien  opera singer diva plava laguna in 1997's  the fifth element  in a rare interview regarding her  extraterrestrial role in the movie  maiwan explained how the fifth element's  french writer director luke pason who  was engaged to her at the time  offered her the part of diva my when  initially passed however saying  oh thank you but if i love you i want to  show you my love that is  pure so i don't want to work with you  vessel ended up hiring a german model to  play diva but she didn't show up to her  makeup test and so my when stepped in to  play the part  my when also revealed that applying the  prosthetics needed to play diva took  three hours every day the team led by  lois burwell applied makeup around  mywen's head  before they glued diva's giant  prosthetic dome onto her own  they then gave my wen stilt and the  dress and  since my wind was so tall in her stilts  she required a special chair  and her own crew to help her eat and  drink  new zealand-born actor jermaine clement  is best known for playing comedic roles  in movies and tv shows such as what we  do in the shadows and flight of the  concords  but he also played a terrifying alien  villain in the 2012 film men in black 3  for which he wore an absolute  ton of prosthetics and makeup and it  took eight hours  so before you even start a work day  you've already had  like what most people think of it as a  as a work day  luckily by the end of the shoot the  makeup team had managed to get that time  down just a little but then they  they gradually got it down to four hours  now we can do it in three hours  legendary makeup artist rick baker who  designed the aliens for men in black  three and its two predecessors  brought forest to life and even made him  scarier than intended in 2012 baker told  digital trends  in the script i got originally he was a  biker but they described him as dennis  hopper from easy rider  i said you know what i think he should  be intimidating like charles manson or  1960s hell's angel president sony barger  i did these designs and kind of  reinvented what i thought he should be  actress model and dancer sophia botella  played the alien warrior jayla in 2016  star trek beyond  her first role that involved prosthetic  makeup while promoting the film boutella  explained to screenslam why she enjoyed  the long makeup process saying  the meditation aspect of it is like  getting into character  you actually take this time sometime you  get on set and you have  very little time i've never done  prosthetics before i like  that second skin i like what it brought  to me it's like as soon as i had it on  you feel in character joel harlow the  movie's makeup designer  explained to inverse in 2017 why  applying makeup to botella  took longer than doing the same to idris  elba who played the film similarly  inhuman looking villain crawl  he said it's deceptively elaborate with  lots of intricate dissections  sofia botella wore a forehead that came  down her cheeks and black design  markings that went all the way down to  her chin  the mouth nose and chin are sofia  otherwise  everything else is all a prosthetic the  time it took  was worth it in the end though because  harlow and fellow makeup artist richard  alonso  both received an oscar nomination for  their work on star trek beyond  british actor and comedian simon pegg  portrayed the slimy alien junk dealer  anker plot in 2015 star wars episode vii  the force awakens  in a 2016 interview with nerdist the  movie's creature supervisor neil scanlon  explained that while they applied  prosthetics to peg during the makeup  process  they also got a little help from the vfx  department he said  i think they did a little bit of cg  enhancement on the inside of the mouth  as well  to give him a slightly wider gape in his  mouth than what you could do in real  life  obviously it would have just been  simon's mouth otherwise even though a  little cgi was used to bring ankar plot  to life  it was nowhere near the amount used for  lupita nyong'o's maz kanata  or andy circus's supreme leader snoke  which were full-blown motion capture  performances  for plut though this successful blend of  cgi and practical effects  helped scamlin and the film's special  effects team earn themselves an academy  award nomination  sadly pegg himself didn't find the suit  all that comfortable  and i had this big rubber like silicone  gauntlets on which were my fingers  and uh when i took them off i could pour  the sweat out  at least you didn't have to wear it for  long australian actor ben mendelsohn has  played  countless villains throughout his long  career but his turn as the alien telos  in 2019's captain marvel  is one of the few roles for which he  actually wore prosthetics and makeup  although he gets to spend a little time  out of makeup in the movie taylor's true  appearance is that of a scrub  a race of green shape-shifting aliens  who are frequently found stirring up  trouble in the marvel universe  to taylor's credit at least he and his  cohorts are revealed to be refugees from  the kree empire halfway through the  events of captain marvel  so it's quite literally not all bad to  throw audiences off that particular  twist  legacy fx supervisor shane mahan made  the film's  skrulls look as intimidating as he could  landing on an appearance similar to that  of their comic book counterparts  when asked about the length of the  makeup process mendelssohn told  entertainment weekly that  in total it only took a couple of hours  when asked if the makeup team managed to  quicken the process at  all mendelson replied they have what do  i do  i sit there no they have they're awesome  it's a couple of hours  it's not that big a deal you know  mendelssohn ended up back in the makeup  chair once more for spider-man far from  home  and will likely don his prosthetics  again as the mcu grows  ever bigger and more cosmic especially  with the upcoming secret invasion series  looming over the horizon  it's a good thing he doesn't seem to  mind scottish stuntman  ray park famously wore a whole heap of  makeup when he portrayed the acrobatic  sith lord darth maul in 1999's  star wars episode 1 the phantom menace  the film's principal makeup artist paul  engelin spoke about maul's devilish look  in a 1999 issue of makeup artist  magazine  he explained the red i used was actually  a water-based aqua color that would  fade but it was quite easy to reapply by  sponging on  the black was real tattoo color which i  had to paint on  it's kind of elasticized so would tend  to peel  rather than run i sponged it on with a  fairly heavily saturated alcohol-based  sponge and  a lot of black pigment even with all of  the action scenes shot out there  it worked in an interview with sci-fi  wire in 2019 park revealed he was  initially unsure about maul's look  explaining  when they were doing me up i just  thought i looked silly you know  my big nose and my weird teeth and then  my blue eyes  and i just felt like a big panda you  know but once the contact lenses were in  and people were staring at me on set it  was like  wow park reprised his royal for a cameo  in 2018  solo a star wars story and provided  motion capture for the character in  the phantom apprentice an episode of the  animated series star wars the clone wars  josh brolin may have donned his motion  capture suit to play the alien villain  thanos in the marvel cinematic universe  but he wasn't actually the first actor  to play the role  in fact american actor and stunt man  damien poitier underwent a round of  prosthetics to portray the mad titan in  a mid-credits stinger at the end of  2012's the avengers  flash forward to 2014 when poitier  explained to the geeks with wives  podcast how he discovered which  character he would play in the avengers  the actor said i found out when i was in  the makeup chair what i was doing  they kept it super quiet because they  didn't want to put any spoilers out  so they kept it super quiet what i was  doing and i didn't find out until they  were casting my face to do the sculpt  although boitie sadly wasn't destined to  play thanos again  he did play hero merc 1 in 2016's  captain america civil war so  that's something at least in 2018 the  costume and creature design powerhouse  iron head studio  led by jose fernandez shared a  behind-the-scenes photo on their  instagram of poitiers wearing the thanos  makeup and prosthetics  as the caption details although thanos  ended up getting a digital sheen for the  film  and eventually became fully digitally  rendered in avengers infinity war jose  still has a soft spot for this practical  makeup design  while the practical thanos makeup was  done away with for later marvel movies  iron head did go on to design costumes  for captain america civil war  as well as a number of other high  profile movies and tv shows including  aquaman and the mandalorian australian  actress elizabeth debicki has starred in  a number of high-profile movies and tv  shows throughout her career but her turn  as the alien queen aisha in 2017's  guardians of the galaxy vol 2 was easily  the most makeup heavy of them all  requiring her to be painted gold from  head to toe while promoting the film  vicki spoke to comicbook.com about  putting on the makeup  she recalled they built a sort of car  wash there was  a lot of paint and a lot of sitting  around and drying  it's quite an intimate process the  film's makeup department head john blake  also spoke to makeup artist magazine  about giving aisha's species the  sovereign their gold look  going into detail about the trouble they  had trying to land on a good color he  explained  there's a lot of gold makeup out there  but some of it doesn't really have a  metallic gleam while others have the  metallic gleam but can look  very textury and crusty so it was just a  matter of mixing batch after batch of  different materials before i could come  up with a gold that had the right amount  of softness and metallic gleam to it  in the end blake and the makeup team  succeeded in giving the sovereign a  bright and visually  arresting gold look one that made them  one of the most  memorable aspects of the entire movie  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite movies are coming soon  sub